cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MissLearn: full-information machine learning from data with meaningful missingness"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Amanda S."
    family-names: Barnard
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4784-2382"
    affiliation: "School of Computing, Australian National University"
version: 0.9.2
date-released: "2026-09-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/amaxiom/MissLearn"
url: "https://github.com/amaxiom/MissLearn"
abstract: >-
  Scikit-learn-style estimators that learn directly from incomplete data by
  full-information maximum likelihood. Each observation contributes exactly
  the features it contains and predictions marginalise over unknown features
  rather than replacing them, so nothing is imputed and nothing is deleted.
  Twelve model families span linear, penalized, kernel, generative,
  Gaussian-process and mixed-effects learners, with tools for missingness
  diagnostics, multiple imputation, exact Shapley-value explanations and
  sensitivity analysis for data missing not at random.
keywords:
  - missing data
  - full information maximum likelihood
  - machine learning
  - scikit-learn
  - imputation
  - Python
